# watch-optout tombstone — suppresses AUTO-provisioning of this slug.
#
# SUPERSEDED REASON (2026-07-27): "dead fork, upstream 404". That was true when a
# stale bare clone worktrees/kriscendobot-garden.git outlived a deleted fork and
# made fork-watch-provisioner.sh re-arm watchers that only FATAL-flapped.
#
# CURRENT REASON (2026-07-28): the slug now names the garden's OWN repo, which was
# TRANSFERRED kriskowal/garden -> kriscendobot/garden. gh api repos/kriscendobot/garden
# returns 200, so the dead-fork rationale no longer holds — but the tombstone must
# STAY, for a different reason:
#
#   * config/fork-owners lists kriscendobot, so the provisioner would now treat the
#     garden's own repo as an own fork and auto-arm BOTH watch sets.
#   * That would add repos/kriscendobot-garden — a COMMIT triager the garden's own
#     repo has never had, which would post jobs off its own main2 commits.
#   * It would also write a default comment-repos/ record, overwriting nothing but
#     competing with the hand-written pr-only arming that keeps the comment-watcher
#     and the issue-inbox from both dispatching on one comment.
#
# The comment surface IS watched, deliberately and by hand: comment-repos/kriscendobot-garden
# (pr-only, sender-gated). repo-watcher.sh reconciles that record into units without
# consulting this file, so this tombstone suppresses ONLY auto-provisioning.
#
# Removing this file would arm a commit triager on the garden's own repo. Do that
# only deliberately. See designs/auto-provision-fork-watchers.md and
# context/operations/repo-transfer.md.
unwatched: kriscendobot/garden (auto-provisioning only — comment surface is hand-armed)
